WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.636
- I would literally be 
sitting in English class and

00:00:02.636 --> 00:00:04.999
reading the Wine Spectator.

00:00:06.596 --> 00:00:08.842
There was just no 
controlling my insanity.

00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:13.030
("Legendary" by Welshly Arms)

00:00:31.702 --> 00:00:32.918
- What if I told you this was

00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:35.535
the last Monday 
morning of your life?

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:43.644
- [Gary] If you think a lot's
happened in the last 10 years

00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:46.313
wait 'til you see what
happens over the next 10 years.

00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:48.115
The stakes are enormously high.

00:00:48.115 --> 00:00:50.517
And I'm not here fear mongering.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.486
This is just what's happening.

00:00:52.486 --> 00:00:54.721
Very honestly, the fact that

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.873
you're the crème 
de la crème of this,

00:00:57.873 --> 00:01:00.480
I assume that the majority of

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.515
people in this 
room are like yes.

00:01:02.515 --> 00:01:03.497
This is the opportunity.

00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:06.733
This is where I transition from
a $6 million a year business to

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.968
$15 million a year business.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:11.271
This is when a transition from
$180,000 a year business to a

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.372
$2.9 million business.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.141
This is pure opportunity.

00:01:14.141 --> 00:01:17.010
The problem is and this is
where everybody defaults into,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.866
they raise their, "Gary, 
I don't grow up with this."

00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:21.784
Me either, Carl.

00:01:21.784 --> 00:01:23.750
(audience laughter)

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.954
I didn't grow up 
with this either, Carl.

00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:28.155
And guess what, Carl?

00:01:28.155 --> 00:01:31.658
You didn't grow up 
driving and you figured it out.

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.461
Understanding the digital
landscape and what our consumers

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:38.365
are doing on it is 
now oxygen for businesses.

00:01:38.365 --> 00:01:39.533
- Awesome.

00:01:39.533 --> 00:01:41.152
- Thank you, darlin'. 
Give me a kiss.

00:01:41.152 --> 00:01:42.903
- Oh.
- [Gary] Take care.

00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:44.071
Thank you for having me.

00:01:44.075 --> 00:01:45.505
- I'm glad you had a nap.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.974
- [Gary] Yes.
I did have a nap.

00:01:46.974 --> 00:01:49.209
Take care.

00:01:51.691 --> 00:01:52.679
Thanks for listening.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.513
Bye guys.
- [Woman] Thank you.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.548
- Thank you for listening.

00:01:54.548 --> 00:01:55.615
Bye, thank you.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.950
Take care, man. 
Thank you, brother.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.251
Thanks, Michael. Bye.

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.923
Let's name it the 
2017 small business talk.

00:02:05.929 --> 00:02:07.472
DRock.

00:02:07.472 --> 00:02:09.353
- [DRock] Gary.

00:02:09.353 --> 00:02:12.749
- Yo, yo, yo, yo, yo, 
Twitter, Twitter, Twitter.

00:02:12.749 --> 00:02:14.490
What's going on?
Good to see you guys.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.949
Morning.

00:02:15.949 --> 00:02:19.709
I'm in Louisiana headed to

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:23.339
Vegas for CES.

00:02:23.339 --> 00:02:26.813
Got a phone call in a few
minutes but just wanted to jump

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:30.913
onto Twitter and 
give you guys some love.

00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:33.387
See how you're doing.

00:02:33.387 --> 00:02:37.610
Maybe we'll jump on a little
bit and see how we do this.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.392
Hope you guys 
are doing super well.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.130
Hope life is good.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:45.474
And yeah, this 
new jacket is fly.

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:47.082
You love it, DRock, right?

00:02:47.082 --> 00:02:48.846
- [DRock] Yeah, 
it's really nice.

00:02:51.554 --> 00:02:52.472
- All good stuff.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.808
Dublin, what's up? 
Good to see you.

00:02:54.808 --> 00:02:56.243
No, Patriots, no way.

00:02:56.243 --> 00:02:58.345
Yeah, anyway.

00:02:58.345 --> 00:02:59.787
See ya.

00:03:02.491 --> 00:03:03.583
This is for you, my friend.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.756
- Oh, that's very 
generous of you.

00:03:04.756 --> 00:03:05.700
- [Gary] Take care of yourself.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.663
- Thank you very much, sir.
I appreciate the courtesy.

00:03:06.663 --> 00:03:07.218
- [Gary] Happy New Year.

00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:07.933
- Alright.
- [Gary] Take care.

00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:08.799
- Watch your step.

00:03:08.799 --> 00:03:11.158
- Gonna try to add 
more context to days.

00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:15.542
In the time that I got off the
stage and drove to this airport,

00:03:15.542 --> 00:03:18.765
one of our big new scopes for
last year got cut in half from

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.701
$2 million to $1 million which
is a problem because the scale

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.749
of the dollars was going to 
help it be more successful and

00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:27.620
one of the CEOs of one of my 
successful startups is having

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.382
some cultural issues where the

00:03:29.382 --> 00:03:33.663
team is struggling 
so that's hard core.

00:03:33.663 --> 00:03:38.585
And so, very quickly in two
seconds two pretty substantial

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:42.884
fires but you take them in the

00:03:42.884 --> 00:03:44.624
micro at the moment and then you

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.677
start leveling them 
up to a macro. Right?

00:03:47.677 --> 00:03:49.696
I take the hit, I absorb it.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:52.211
Now I'm thinking, I'm pondering,

00:03:52.211 --> 00:03:54.835
and now I'm already 
strategizing on how to fix it.

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:58.105
I think way too many people
spend too much time dwelling and

00:03:58.105 --> 00:04:00.474
they allow something like this
to ruin their day or ruin their

00:04:00.474 --> 00:04:03.410
week or ruin their 
month or ruin their year.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.878
I think one of the things

00:04:04.878 --> 00:04:07.013
I talk about is 
having a stomach,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.865
having the 
stomach for this game.

00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:11.985
This is exactly what I refer to.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:16.677
I've been around a lot of
executives and a lot of partners

00:04:16.677 --> 00:04:18.524
who would use something like

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:23.263
this as a day-ender 
as I call it.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.875
I've come to realize how much
of a strength that is of mine of

00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:29.469
putting things in 
the proper context and

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.127
dealing with reality.

00:04:31.127 --> 00:04:32.906
You know, when 
you're an entrepreneur

00:04:32.906 --> 00:04:34.207
you're a firefighter.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.876
Especially if you're 
the last line of defense.

00:04:35.876 --> 00:04:36.723
It's all on you.

00:04:36.723 --> 00:04:39.412
There's no punting it down.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.848
Right now we have a 
potential conflict issue of

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.983
which account do we go to.

00:04:42.983 --> 00:04:45.886
I'm trying to keep 
Marcus off as a CEO,

00:04:45.886 --> 00:04:47.887
give me a day, give me a day.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:49.589
The truth is I'm not 
accomplishing anything here.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.053
I'm just thinking, I'm trying to
ponder but the quicker you make

00:04:52.053 --> 00:04:55.875
actions, the quicker you 
can adjust to negativity,

00:04:55.875 --> 00:05:00.500
big blows, 
medium blows, large blows.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:04.304
The turnaround speed in
your adjustment to an issue is

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:07.774
usually an unbelievable proxy to
the level of success you'll have

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:08.809
as an entrepreneur.

00:05:08.809 --> 00:05:11.444
So you need to start 
conditioning yourself for the

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.809
emotional war that 
entrepreneurship is.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.469
- [DRock] What 
are you doing now?

00:05:22.469 --> 00:05:26.560
- [Gary] Right now, I'm 
answering an AMA for Mogul,

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.295
a media site that 
I'm an investor in.

00:05:28.295 --> 00:05:32.966
Great entrepreneur, she asked me
and it's really not what I want

00:05:32.966 --> 00:05:36.703
to be using my time on but 
I think you have to come through

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:41.013
for the partnerships you make
and so she doesn't ask often and

00:05:41.013 --> 00:05:43.113
so even though it's a tough
week and things of that nature,

00:05:43.113 --> 00:05:46.605
I'm doing this AMA on 
their site on OnMogul.com

00:05:46.605 --> 00:05:48.515
and OnMogul.com

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:50.881
and cranking away at answers,
just trying to get through a

00:05:50.881 --> 00:05:53.620
bunch so I can get 
through security here.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.356
Somebody asked me about a
time in my life when I was going

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:58.458
through a struggle 
and how I got through.

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:02.963
And it made me think about 2005
when I turned 30 and I realized

00:06:02.963 --> 00:06:07.000
that my actions were 
not backing up my words.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.335
I've said that 
a couple of times,

00:06:08.335 --> 00:06:10.270
if you have the audacity to
dream you have to make your

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.405
actions, you have to do it.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.874
And I had a moment like that.

00:06:13.874 --> 00:06:14.874
I was very successful.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.245
I built a huge business and
I would say from 28 to 30

00:06:18.245 --> 00:06:20.884
I probably got caught in 
to some form of complacency.

00:06:20.884 --> 00:06:22.904
We were growing like crazy.

00:06:22.904 --> 00:06:24.709
But it was complacent compared

00:06:24.709 --> 00:06:26.757
to the ambition that I set out

00:06:26.757 --> 00:06:30.954
to accomplish and so from 
28 to 30 I was building a

00:06:30.954 --> 00:06:33.284
big business, a big wine
e-commerce business.

00:06:33.284 --> 00:06:36.119
I was innovating, I was hustling

00:06:36.119 --> 00:06:38.189
but I wasn't working 
as hard as I am now.

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:41.723
I wasn't doing strategically 
smart things that were

00:06:41.723 --> 00:06:43.341
gonna allow me to achieve the

00:06:43.341 --> 00:06:45.228
professional things 
that I wanted.

00:06:45.228 --> 00:06:47.244
And I wasn't so
over-capitalizing on my

00:06:47.244 --> 00:06:49.234
family time with Lizzie 
in return either.

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:51.872
So it wasn't like I was 
getting some amazing benefit.

00:06:51.872 --> 00:06:54.963
And so, 28 to 30 was an
interesting time for me because

00:06:54.963 --> 00:06:58.215
I think that there was so
much success so fast that I got

00:06:58.215 --> 00:07:02.311
caught for 24 months of maybe
not hustling as hard and as

00:07:02.311 --> 00:07:05.637
smart as I could 
and more importantly,

00:07:05.637 --> 00:07:07.296
on my 30th birthday I realized

00:07:07.296 --> 00:07:09.935
I wasn't gonna 
buy the New York Jets.

00:07:09.935 --> 00:07:12.609
And that's kind of weirdly okay

00:07:12.609 --> 00:07:14.763
as you guys know I 
want that but that's okay.

00:07:14.763 --> 00:07:17.664
What crushed me 
was I was full of shit.

00:07:17.665 --> 00:07:21.015
I wasn't putting in the work

00:07:21.015 --> 00:07:24.127
at a macro and 
micro level to give

00:07:24.127 --> 00:07:26.886
me a chance to 
buy the New York Jets.

00:07:26.886 --> 00:07:28.789
Just got in to Vegas.

00:07:28.789 --> 00:07:30.957
Connected in Houston.

00:07:30.957 --> 00:07:34.469
Waiting for DRock 
to come off the plane.

00:07:34.469 --> 00:07:38.901
CES for a couple days, day and a
half and then back on the grind.

00:07:38.901 --> 00:07:42.064
Going to Seattle to try and
sign a kid for VaynerSports.

00:07:42.064 --> 00:07:43.763
Just did a bunch of email,

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:46.549
the eBay challenge 
is out of control.

00:07:46.549 --> 00:07:48.902
The 21 Savage moment 
in The #AskGaryVee Show

00:07:48.902 --> 00:07:50.226
caught people's attention.

00:07:50.226 --> 00:07:52.428
So, what's going on.

00:07:52.428 --> 00:07:56.322
The ambition I have and the
excitement I have is the process

00:07:56.322 --> 00:08:00.046
of trying to buy the New York
Jets versus buying them and so

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:04.067
yeah, I think that era was
interesting to me and so when

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:07.354
I tell you your actions 
have to backup your words,

00:08:07.354 --> 00:08:10.523
I come from a place of 
experience 'cause I lived a

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:13.478
couple years 
there where I didn't.

00:08:13.478 --> 00:08:17.797
And I know what it tastes like
and I got into a place where

00:08:17.797 --> 00:08:21.234
I really spoke myself 
from November 14th, 2005

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:25.041
through probably 
January 15th, 2005

00:08:25.041 --> 00:08:28.011
and then February 20, 2006,

00:08:28.011 --> 00:08:31.250
February 2005, I started 
Wine Library TV and started

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.344
taking the internet 
more seriously and

00:08:33.344 --> 00:08:35.786
the rest was history.

00:08:35.786 --> 00:08:38.974
(light music)

